Representative Data Verification (Methodology)

To verify the integrity and reproducibility of the electrophysiological processing pipeline, summary N400 amplitude values were exported for one representative participant per group — Sub-01 from the experimental group (EG) and Sub-21 from the active control group (CG) — across all three longitudinal assessment timepoints (Months 1, 3, and 6). Each record was stored as a MATLAB Level 5 (.mat) file containing five documented variables: subject_id, group, month, n400_amplitude_uv (double precision, in microvolts), and a status field set to verified_sample (S1–S6).

All six files were validated programmatically prior to inclusion in the supplementary material. The validation routine confirmed: (a) scalar integrity, with all numeric fields finite (no NaN or Inf values) and of the expected type (int64 for identifiers and timepoints; float64 for amplitudes); (b) schema consistency, with an identical five-variable structure across all files; and (c) metadata–filename consistency, with the embedded subject_id, group, and month values matching the naming convention sub-NN_GG_Mn in every case (S1–S6).

The extracted values were as follows. The representative EG participant exhibited a monotonic reduction in N400 negativity from −5.15 µV at baseline (Month 1) to −3.49 µV at Month 3 and −1.44 µV at Month 6 — an attenuation of approximately 72% over the six-month interval, following a nearly linear trajectory (S1; S2; S3). In contrast, the CG participant remained largely stable across the same period (−5.58 µV at Month 1, −5.18 µV at Month 3, and −5.13 µV at Month 6; total change ≈ 0.45 µV, with the trajectory flattening after Month 3) (S4; S5; S6). The divergent single-subject trajectories are illustrated in the accompanying publication-quality figure (300 dpi) (S7). All amplitudes were negative, consistent with standard N400 scoring conventions in which the component is quantified as a negative-going deflection in microvolts.

These single-subject trajectories are presented solely for methodological illustration and pipeline verification; they do not substitute for the group-level linear mixed-effects analysis (N = 40) reported in the main manuscript. Furthermore, the archived files contain extracted ERP component summary values, not raw time-series waveforms, and should accordingly be cited as extracted component values for representative samples rather than representative waveforms (S1–S7).

Data Availability Statement

Representative processed ERP outputs (N400 amplitude summary values in MATLAB .mat format) for one participant per experimental group (Sub-01, EG; Sub-21, CG) across all three assessment timepoints (Months 1, 3, and 6) (S1; S2; S3; S4; S5; S6), together with the complete reproducible analysis pipeline (LMM specification and figure-generation scripts) (S7), are provided in the Supplementary Material. Due to ethical restrictions concerning clinical language-learning data, the full longitudinal electrophysiological dataset (N = 40) is not publicly archived; it is available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request, in accordance with the FAIR data principles.

